  "narrative": {
    "intro": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance is a federal contractor with $14.5B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. TriWest Healthcare Alliance has 25 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $581M, and obligations are up 8.6% year over year. TriWest Healthcare Alliance has grown from $6.7B in FY21 to $14.5B in FY26, with a notable jump to $13.4B in FY25. TriWest Healthcare Alliance sells primarily to health-focused federal buyers, led by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $9.8B and the Department of Defense at $4.7B. TriWest Healthcare Alliance operates mainly in Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers, which accounts for $14.2B, with a smaller presence in Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds at $288M. TriWest Healthcare Alliance current-year totals are fiscal year to date and partial. TriWest Healthcare Alliance figures for awards in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values, while the other figures are contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are TriWest Healthcare Alliance customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $9.8B to TriWest Healthcare Alliance. The Department of Defense is the second buyer, obligating $4.7B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the dominant market for TriWest Healthcare Alliance at $14.2B, with Pharmacy Benefit Management and related services at $288M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations changed recently?",
        "body": "TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations rose from $6.7B in FY21 to $14.5B in FY26. TriWest Healthcare Alliance obligations increased to $13.4B in FY25 before reaching $14.5B in FY26, and obligations are up 8.6% year over year. TriWest Healthcare Alliance currently shows 25 awards for the fiscal year to date with an average award size of $581M."
      }
    ]
  },
